# Everything that goes into the tarball but is not a source of a program or an
# installed data file. The packaging directories are listed file by file on
# purpose: naming the directory itself makes automake copy whatever happens to
# be in it at "make dist" time, which for windows/ would mean the multi-gigabyte
# mxe/ build tree, and for the others the generated files (configure output,
# build leftovers). The lists below are the files under version control, so a
# tarball built from a dirty work tree is the same as one built from a fresh
# checkout. Files generated by configure - windows/*.exe.manifest and the
# windows/installer*.nsi - are deliberately absent; their *.in templates are
# here instead.
EXTRA_DIST = 	iniparser/LICENSE \
			COPYING \
			README \
			debian/changelog \
			debian/control \
			debian/copyright \
			debian/docs \
			debian/pica-client.install \
			debian/pica-client.menu \
			debian/pica-client.postinst \
			debian/pica-client.postrm \
			debian/pica-client.preinst \
			debian/pica-client.prerm \
			debian/pica-node.default \
			debian/pica-node.dirs \
			debian/pica-node.init \
			debian/pica-node.install \
			debian/pica-node.postinst \
			debian/pica-node.postrm \
			debian/pica-node.preinst \
			debian/pica-node.prerm \
			debian/rules \
			debian/source/format \
			gentoo/gentoo_initscript \
